From 9548ee624952dc3d4c11d85864caae087c20bbab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:54:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: DLSS super resolution and DLAA at the end of
 the scene (PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL=dlss)

rsx_temporal: the title's camera hands each frame's view-projection
(without jitter) and its jitter to the backend, tagged with the flips
queued so far, which is the count the drain has reached while that
frame is drawn (cellGcm_frame_queued / _reached); a Halton 2,3 jitter
sequence over half a render pixel, 8 phases per output pixel.

Backend: viewport and scissor scale with the target drawn into, so a
target can have a size of its own. At the copy of the finished display
buffer (the MLAA hook) the scene, drawn at DLSS's render size, goes
through NGX with the world's depth (copied before the title clears it
for the first-person model), motion vectors from the camera
(rsx_vk_motion.comp; the first-person model does not move) and the
jitter; the output-size image becomes the display buffer's until it is
presented, so the HUD is drawn over it at the output size. The MLAA
does not run under DLSS.

rsx_vk_dlss.cpp is a stub unless CMake gets PS3RECOMP_DLSS_SDK; the SDK
and its library stay out of the repository.

