+/* Temporal upscaling (PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL=dlss), at the end of the scene: the
+ * copy of the finished display buffer the MLAA hook is on, before the HUD.
+ *
+ * The scene is drawn at the render size, smaller than the output (or the
+ * same, DLAA). Here DLSS takes it, with the world's depth (copied before the
+ * title cleared it for the first-person model, s_tmz), motion vectors from
+ * the camera (rsx_vk_motion.comp, the records of rsx_temporal.h) and the
+ * frame's jitter, and writes the output-size picture. That image then becomes
+ * the display buffer's own, so the HUD is drawn over it at the output size
+ * (viewport and scissor follow the target), and after the buffer is presented
+ * it gets its render-size image back for the next scene. The MLAA does not
+ * run: DLSS antialiases. Motion blur is not drawn (it is made at 1280x720).
+ *
+ * PS3RECOMP_DLSS_MODE=quality (default) | balanced | performance | ultra | dlaa.
+ * PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL_DUMP=<dir>: while <dir>/go exists, each frame's colour,
+ * world depth and camera record are written there (with
+ * PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL_DUMP_EVERY=<n>, three frames in a row out of n), to
+ * check the camera data against the pictures. */
+#define VK_TM_SWAPS 4
